description:
***Role***
: Manager / Assistant Manager — Membership & Operations (Full-time)

***Reports to***
: Director, IPSO

***Job Location***
: IPSO Office, Begumpet, Hyderabad (On-site)

***Experience***
: 5–8 years

***Level***
: Assistant Manager or Manager (title and grade to match the candidate)

***Function***
: Membership, Operations, Events

**About IPSO**

IPSO is the national, not-for-profit industry body representing India’s Contract Research, Development and Manufacturing Organisation (CRDMO) sector. Founded by India’s leading CRDMO companies, it works on policy advocacy, ecosystem development, talent, and global engagement to help make India the preferred global destination for contract research, development, and manufacturing.

The Secretariat is being built now. This is an early, foundational role: you will work directly with the Director, as well as the Co-Presidents and member companies. It suits someone who wants ownership, variety, and the chance to help build an institution from the ground up.

**The role in one line**

*To be the Secretariat’s core execution engine — running membership, operations, and events smoothly, and supporting the policy and communications work.*

**Key responsibilities**

**1. Membership management**
(primary)

•     Manage the full membership lifecycle: enquiries, applications, onboarding, renewals, and records;

•     Serve as the day-to-day point of contact for member companies and their representatives;

•     Maintain the register of members, membership files, and the membership database;

•     Coordinate committees and working groups — scheduling, papers, minutes, and follow-up actions;

•     Track member engagement and help keep members active and satisfied.

**2. Operations & administration**
(primary)

•     Run the day-to-day operations of the Secretariat office; Coordinate with vendors and support partners;

•     Maintain records, registers, and the compliance calendar, supporting the Director on governance filings;

•     Help prepare budgets, track expenses, and support financial administration with the accounts partner;

•     Organise meetings of the Executive Committee and General Body, including notices, agendas, and minutes.

**3. Events & stakeholder engagement**

•     Plan and execute IPSO events — roundtables, summits, member meets, and delegations — end to end;

•     Manage logistics, venues, invitations, speakers, and on-the-day coordination;

•     Support engagement with government, industry, academia, and ecosystem partners.

**4. Policy & communications support**
(supporting, with room to grow)

•     Coordinate member consultations and surveys, and help compile responses into clear summaries;

•     Draft and edit letters, notes, member communications, newsletters, and website content;

•     Support the preparation of policy submissions, position papers, and reports led by the Director, Co-Presidents, and members;

•     Keep track of relevant sector, regulatory, and policy developments.

***Who we are looking for***

**Essential**

•     5–8 years of relevant work experience;

•     A proven ability to manage many moving parts, many stakeholders, and deadlines without dropping things;

•     Able to draft clear letters, minutes, notes, and member communications with little supervision;

•     Event management experience: having planned and run professional events or meetings end to end;

•     Good interpersonal skills and executive presence — comfortable dealing with senior industry leaders;

•     Comfort with MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and everyday digital tools.

**Highly preferred**
(any one of these makes a candidate stand out)

•     Industry-body / trade-association experience — the strongest fit. Prior work at industry associations;

•     Membership-organisation experience of any kind (professional bodies, chambers, councils) and Incubators;

•     A pharma / life-sciences connection: either direct experience in a pharma, biotech, CRDMO company or Pharma media, close exposure to the sector will be an advantage;

**Personal qualities**

•     Self-starter who takes ownership and works well with little supervision;

•     Organised, reliable, and detail-oriented;

•     Discreet and trustworthy with confidential member information;

•     Collaborative, service-minded, and comfortable in a small, hands-on team;

•     Willing to travel and to take on a wide, evolving remit as IPSO grows.

**Qualifications**

•     Any Graduate degree required with relevant experience;

**What the role offers**

•     A rare chance to help build a national industry body from its earliest days;

•     Direct exposure to the leadership of India’s top CRDMO companies and to national policy work;

•     A broad, varied remit with real ownership and visible impact; Room to grow as the Secretariat expands.

**HOW TO APPLY﻿**

Please send your CV and a short covering note explaining your fit for this role to director@ipso.in, with the subject line “Application — Manager, Membership & Operations”.

**Job Summary**
**JOB DESCRIPTION**
 The Territory Account Manager is responsible for selling Masimo’s Acute Care product portfolio and developing strategic relationships with a variety of clinical leaders in targeted hospitals. This position is a proactive member of the sales team that will facilitate securing new business and growing existing business in their assigned territory.




**Duties \& Responsibilities**
* Utilize Masimo’s established sales process to convert competitive accounts to Masimo technology;
* Utilize CRM to track all opportunities and update on a weekly basis at a minimum;
* Conduct demonstrations (side by side) and evaluations (using ADC) for Masimo technologies;
* Conduct and assist clinical specialists with Physical Inventories as part of the sales process;
* Conduct Presentations that discuss Masimo’s value proposition;
* Drives capital products sales in assigned Masimo territory for:
+ Pulse CO\-Oximetry
+ Rainbow
+ Patient Safety Net
+ Capnography
+ Brain Function Monitoring

* Identify and develop working relationships with clinical thought leaders at strategic accounts to position the benefits in care processes and patients outcomes of Masimo’s wireless Pulse CO\-Oximetry and Floor Monitoring solutions;
* Drives to conclusion Masimo Sensor agreements for both new conversions and renewing existing accounts;
* Actively be able to articulate information in clinical studies regarding Masimo technologies;
* Collaborates with Masimo Team Members including Corporate Accounts, IDN and Clinical Specialist, where team selling is appropriate, and provides critical information to marketing and upper management including market trends and competitive activity;
* Maintains high skill level in Strategic and Tactical selling skills;
* Organizes and conducts user seminars on the compelling needs and benefits of Pulse CO\-Oximetry and Floor Monitoring, and helps clinicians minimize the quantity of sentinel events on the floors;
* Collaborates with the Clinical Team to coordinate clinical evaluations of Masimo’s Rainbow SET Pulse CO\-Oximetry technology to establish for vocal, credible clinical champions (VCCCs);
* Create and maintain CRM database of key account information including key account profiles with updates on:
+ current status and next steps in establishing targeted VCCCs
+ list of sales opportunities with a realistic sales forecast data

* Must be able to travel and stay away overnight;
* Performs special projects as requested


**Minimum Qualifications**
* At least 5 years of solid B2B sales with a track record of exceeding quota;
* Experience with medical device or related industry
* Experience with critical care or related area would be advantageous
* Formal training or studies in art of selling;
* Demonstrated, quantifiable sales ability;
* Team Player;
* Strong sense of ambition, self\-motivation and self\-discipline;
* Superior written and verbal communication skills and exceptional ability to lead group presentations;
* Successful history managing customer interactions, with excellent organizational and time management skills;
* Travel and overnight stays are required, as well as a valid driver’s license


**Preferred Qualifications**
* Background knowledge of Hospital IT and EMR connectivity a plus;
* Background knowledge of selling in the hospital environment a plus;


**Education**
 Bachelor’s degree is required
